{"path":"experimental/ranges/concepts/Relation","title":"std::experimental::ranges::Relation","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::experimental::ranges::</span>Relation","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/experimental/ranges/concepts/Relation","section":"experimental","kind":"page","summary":"The concept Relation<R, T, U> specifies that R defines a binary relation over the set of expressions whose type and value category are those encoded by either T or U.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/cpp/header/experimental/ranges/concepts\">&lt;experimental/ranges/concepts&gt;</a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-ranges\" id=\"Version_1\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> R, <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> T, <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> U <span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><br>concept <span class=\"kw4\">bool</span> Relation <span class=\"sy1\">=</span><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; Predicate<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>R, T, T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> <span class=\"sy3\">&amp;&amp;</span><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; Predicate<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>R, U, U<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> <span class=\"sy3\">&amp;&amp;</span><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; CommonReference<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/types/remove_reference\"><span class=\"kw612\">std::<span class=\"me2\">remove_reference_t</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span>,<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/types/remove_reference\"><span class=\"kw612\">std::<span class=\"me2\">remove_reference_t</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>U<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> <span class=\"sy3\">&amp;&amp;</span><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; Predicate<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>R,<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; <a href=\"/w/cpp/experimental/ranges/type_traits/common_reference\"><span class=\"kw2837\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">common_reference_t</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/types/remove_reference\"><span class=\"kw612\">std::<span class=\"me2\">remove_reference_t</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span>,<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/types/remove_reference\"><span class=\"kw612\">std::<span class=\"me2\">remove_reference_t</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>U<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span>,<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; <a href=\"/w/cpp/experimental/ranges/type_traits/common_reference\"><span class=\"kw2837\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">common_reference_t</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/types/remove_reference\"><span class=\"kw612\">std::<span class=\"me2\">remove_reference_t</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span>,<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/types/remove_reference\"><span class=\"kw612\">std::<span class=\"me2\">remove_reference_t</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>U<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;&gt;</span> <span class=\"sy3\">&amp;&amp;</span><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; Predicate<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>R, T, U<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> <span class=\"sy3\">&amp;&amp;</span><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; Predicate<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>R, U, T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (1) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-ranges-ts t-mark-ts\">(ranges TS)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>The concept <code>Relation&lt;R, T, U&gt;</code> specifies that <code>R</code> defines a binary relation over the set of expressions whose type and value category are those encoded by either <code>T</code> or <code>U</code>.\n</p><p>Given\n</p>\n<ul><li> <code>r</code>, an expression such that <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">decltype<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>r<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code> is <code>R</code>,\n</li><li> <code>t</code>, an expression such that <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">decltype<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>t<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code> is <code>T</code>,\n</li><li> <code>u</code>, an expression such that <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">decltype<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>u<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code> is <code>U</code>,\n</li></ul>\n<p>and let <code>C</code> be <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/experimental/ranges/type_traits/common_reference\"><span class=\"kw2837\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">common_reference_t</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/types/remove_reference\"><span class=\"kw612\">std::<span class=\"me2\">remove_reference_t</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span>, <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/types/remove_reference\"><span class=\"kw612\">std::<span class=\"me2\">remove_reference_t</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>U<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span></span></code>,\n</p><p>then <code>Relation&lt;R, T, U&gt;</code> is satisfied only if\n</p>\n<ul><li> <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">bool</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>r<span class=\"br0\">(</span>t, u<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> <span class=\"kw4\">bool</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>r<span class=\"br0\">(</span>C<span class=\"br0\">(</span>t<span class=\"br0\">)</span>, C<span class=\"br0\">(</span>u<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code> and\n</li><li> <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">bool</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>r<span class=\"br0\">(</span>u, t<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> <span class=\"kw4\">bool</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>r<span class=\"br0\">(</span>C<span class=\"br0\">(</span>u<span class=\"br0\">)</span>, C<span class=\"br0\">(</span>t<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>.\n</li></ul>","headings":[],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"experimental","title":"Experimental C++ Features"},{"path":"experimental/ranges","title":"Extensions for ranges"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::experimental::ranges::Relation","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration. The concept Relation<R, T, U> specifies that R defines a binary relation over the set of expressions whose type and…"}]},"standards":[],"wordCount":133,"codeBlockCount":0}
